{"file":"QA Bug Hunter-1.9.0-v2.zip","bytes":100826,"status":"已读取","plugins":[{"path":".claude-plugin/plugin.json","name":"qa-bug-hunter","displayName":"QA Bug Hunter","description":"Finds, reproduces, and confirms bugs in frontend or backend code and reports them with evidence — read-only on your codebase (it never fixes). Confirms via the project's own unit tests; an optional Playwright MCP, enabled on demand, handles UI verification.","version":"1.9.0","license":"MIT","repository":"https://github.com/MartinHar/qa-bug-hunter","homepage":"https://github.com/MartinHar/qa-bug-hunter","keywords":["qa","testing","bug-hunting","playwright","code-review","quality-assurance","security"]}],"skills":[{"path":"skills/qa-bug-hunter/SKILL.md","name":"qa-bug-hunter","description":"Find, reproduce, and confirm bugs in a codebase and report them with evidence — a read-only QA pass that never modifies code. ALWAYS use this skill when the request carries any bug-finding intent — find / hunt / audit for bugs, QA a target, reproduce or confirm a specific bug — INCLUDING when that same request also asks for a fix. \"Find the bug in X and fix it\" and \"audit this module and fix what you find\" ARE bug hunts and DO use this skill: hunt, confirm and report the bug with evidence, then decline the fix as out of scope and never modify the code. Asking for a fix alongside the finding never disqualifies a request — only the total absence of bug-finding intent does. Examples that use this skill: \"find bugs in X\", \"QA this PR\", \"audit this module for defects\", \"reproduce this bug\", \"is this a bug?\", \"find the bug in X and fix it\". It does NOT apply when nothing is being hunted — building, implementing, refactoring, or repairing an already-identified problem (\"fix the login bug\", \"this crashes, fix it\", \"add pagination\") — where it is inert and must not constrain the work or other tools.","headings":["QA Bug Hunter","What this skill is for — and what it is not","Rules that govern the whole run","The working folder","Before hunting — clarify only what's needed","The workflow","0. Establish ground truth","1. Risk-rank the surface","2. Form precise hypotheses","3. Confirm with a unit test (primary path)","4. Escalate to the browser only when a unit test can't see it","5. Write the report to a file","6. Update the knowledge base","Guardrails"],"name_hint":"qa · bug · hunter","description_zh":"只读查找、复现并确认代码缺陷，以证据报告结果而不改代码；原说明即使请求同时要求修复，也将修复排除在此技能范围，已明确问题的单纯修复不属于缺陷搜寻。"}],"commands":[{"path":"commands/hunt.md","name":"hunt","description":"Start a QA bug hunt — find, reproduce, and confirm bugs (read-only, never fixes)","headings":[]}],"readmes":[{"path":"README.md","headings":["QA Bug Hunter","How it behaves (the rules)","Cross-service awareness (on demand)","The `qa-bug-hunt/` working folder","Permissions & data","Install","The browser (only for UI bugs) — handled for you","Auth in 30 seconds","How to use it","Hunt a remote repo by URL","Example run (shape)","Evals","Recommended companions","Customizing","Layout"]},{"path":"evals/README.md","headings":["Evals","Two ways to check the plugin","1. Structural checks — free, no tokens, run anytime","2. Behavioral evals — runs the plugin, spends tokens","Scenario contract","What each scenario guards"]},{"path":"hooks/README.md","headings":["Optional read-only enforcement (OFF by default)","Should you enable it?","Recommended: a dedicated hunt session (no rename, nothing left enabled)","Enable persistently (rename)","then /reload-plugins (CLI) or restart Claude Code","Disable again","then reload / restart"]},{"path":"evals/04-resource-memory/fixture/README.md","headings":["Fixture for the resource-memory eval"]}],"mcp_servers":[],"config_names":[],"paths":[".claude-plugin/marketplace.json",".claude-plugin/plugin.json",".gitignore","CHANGELOG.md","CLAUDE.md","INSTALL.md","LICENSE","README.md","agents/partition-scanner.md","commands/hunt.md","evals/01-planted-bug/SCENARIO.md","evals/01-planted-bug/check